Assertions:
[STATUS] The request answers 200 with succeeded=true {OBSERVED}
[STATUS] The first grant answers 200 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] The first grant carries access_token {OBSERVED}
[STATUS] The second grant with the same code answers 400 {SPEC}
[BODY] The second response carries error invalid_grant and NO access_token - the same refusal as a wrong or expired code {SPEC}
[STATUS] currentuser with firstToken answers 200 and identifies the account {OBSERVED}

Preconditions:
Re-arm the disposable account FIRST: node scripts/seed-data/auth/seed-otp-signin.mjs --verify (re-arms the disposable account: unlock + failed-attempt count 0)
@td(OTP_LOCKOUT_USER_1.email) is used by THIS case only (no other case shares it); OtpSignIn.Enabled is on for {{STORE_ID}}; platform lockout threshold N is the IdentityOptions:Lockout failed-attempt limit (observed 5, 120 s lock on vcptcore_qa1)
Sign-in log recording is enabled (Settings > Platform > Sign In Log > Record sign-in attempts = On)

Assertions:
[STATUS] Attempts 1..N-1 answer 400 invalid_grant with code invalid_code {OBSERVED}
[BODY] After N wrong codes the account is locked: attempt N+1 answers code user_is_temporary_locked_out with lockoutSecondsRemaining > 0 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] The correct code is refused while locked - no access_token {OBSERVED}
[STATUS] After lockoutSecondsRemaining has elapsed the correct code (still inside its lifetime) signs in with 200 {SPEC}
[BODY] The attempt on which the lock engages is reported with a lockout code or invalid_code - record which, no attempt returns a token {SPEC}
[BODY] The sign-in log has signInType=OTP rows for the account: wrong codes with failureReason InvalidCode, the locked attempt with failureReason LockedOut {OBSERVED}

Preconditions:
Re-arm the disposable account FIRST: node scripts/seed-data/auth/seed-otp-signin.mjs --verify (re-arms the disposable account: unlock + failed-attempt count 0)
@td(OTP_LOCKOUT_USER_2.email) is used by THIS case only (a different account from the lockout case) and has password {{DEFAULT_TEST_PASSWORD}}; threshold N as in the lockout case (observed 5)
OtpSignIn.Enabled is on for {{STORE_ID}}

Assertions:
[STATUS] Attempts 1..4 are refused with 400 and no token {OBSERVED}
[BODY] After 3 password + 2 code failures (N=5 in total) the account is locked: the correct password is refused with a lockout error and no access_token {OBSERVED}
[BODY] The correct code is refused too, with user_is_temporary_locked_out and lockoutSecondsRemaining > 0 {OBSERVED}
[STATE] Lockout was reached by the COMBINED count: neither 3 password failures nor 2 code failures alone can lock it, so a locked account proves one shared counter {SPEC}

[STATUS] Both requests answer 200 with succeeded=true {OBSERVED}
[BODY] Two OtpSignInEmailNotification messages exist, one per request {OBSERVED}
[STATUS] The code from the latest message signs in with 200 {OBSERVED}
[STATE] Record sameCode: inside one time window a resend yields the SAME code (observed; open PO question - the UI says "New code sent." while nothing new was issued); if the codes differ, record whether code1 is still accepted {OBSERVED}

[BODY] The request after the switch answers error.code otp_disabled {OBSERVED}
[STATUS] The pre-switch code is refused with 400 and code otp_disabled {OBSERVED}
[BODY] The refusal carries no access_token {OBSERVED}
[BODY] The sign-in log has a signInType=OTP row with failureReason OtpDisabled {OBSERVED}

[STATE] The fixture is decidable: homeStore is in trusted and differs from {{STORE_ID}} {SPEC}
[STATUS] The request answers 200 with succeeded=true {OBSERVED}
[STATUS] The grant answers 200 with access_token {OBSERVED}
[BODY] currentuser identifies the account and its storeId equals homeStore (the buyer keeps their home store) {OBSERVED}

[BODY] The request is refused with error.code user_cannot_login_in_store and succeeded=false (a masked answer when DetailedErrors is off) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] after equals before: NO sign-in email is sent to a contact of another store or to an account with no store {OBSERVED}
[STATUS] The grant answers 400 and carries no access_token {SPEC}
[BODY] The grant never signs the account into {{STORE_ID}} {SPEC}

[BODY] msg.subject is exactly "Your sign-in code" with no trailing whitespace or line break {OBSERVED}
[BODY] msg.body contains the 6-digit code inside <strong>...</strong> {OBSERVED}
[BODY] msg.from is set and equals storeEmail - the same sender a store password-reset email carries {SPEC}
[BODY] msg is addressed to {{USER_EMAIL}} {OBSERVED}

[BODY] The wrong-code row has signInType="OTP", succeeded=false and failureReason InvalidCode {OBSERVED}
[BODY] The success row has signInType="OTP", succeeded=true and an empty failureReason {OBSERVED}
[BODY] Neither row is typed Password {OBSERVED}
[BODY] Both rows carry createdDate, ipAddress and userAgent {OBSERVED}

[STATUS] Each request body with a missing field answers 400, not 500 {OBSERVED}
[STATUS] The malformed JSON body answers 400 and the response carries no stack trace {OBSERVED}
[BODY] The unknown store answers error.code store_not_found {OBSERVED}
[BODY] Each grant with a missing parameter answers 400 and carries no access_token {OBSERVED}
[BODY] No response body contains an exception type name or a stack trace {SPEC}

[STATE] The account is blocked: lockoutEnd is in the future {OBSERVED}
[STATE] after equals before: NO sign-in code is sent to an administrator-blocked account, whatever PasswordLogin:DetailedErrors says {SPEC}
[BODY] The request is refused (succeeded=false) or answered with the masked outcome, but never creates a message {SPEC}
